@page "/KerryShaleBook"

<PageTitle>Kerry Shale Fanpage: Kerry Shale</PageTitle>

<style>
	@@import url('css/booklet/normalize.css');
	@@import url('wow_book/wow_book.css');
	@@import url('css/booklet/main.css');
</style>

<div>
	<div class="book-container">
		<div id="booklet">
			<div class="text-center p-1 h-100 align-content-center bg-black text-white">
				<img src="/images/booklet/KS.jpg" alt="The older Kerry Shale" class="mh-70" /><br />
				Kerry Shale
			</div>
			<div class="text-center p-1 h-100 align-content-center bg-black text-white">
				&nbsp;
			</div>
			<div class="text-center p-1 h-100 align-content-center">
				Once upon a time...
			</div>
			<div class="text-center p-1 h-100 align-content-center">
				On a summer day in 1946, a young gentleman impishly pulled one of the pigtails of a young lady at Winnipeg Beach. This gesture would end up for both in meeting the love of their life. 
				He was born in Canada in 1926. She was born in Poland in 1928 and immigrated to Canada only 3 years later. They married on 2 January 1949.
			</div>
			<div class="text-center p-1 h-100 align-content-center">
				<img src="/images/booklet/KS_parents.jpg" alt="Kerry Shale's parents" class="mh-70" /><br />
				<p class="font-smaller">Kerry Shale's parents,<br />married since 75+ years</p>
			</div>
			<div class="text-center p-1 h-100 align-content-center">
				Three children were born, two boys and a girl. One of those two boys, the older one, would become a famous actor and voice artist later: His name is Kerry Shale, he was born in 1952.
				He moved to Vancouver and studied acting there. He would work at Studio 58. In the year 1978, he got an job offer in London (UK) which he could not reject.
			</div>
			<div class="text-center p-1 h-100 align-content-center">
				<img src="/images/booklet/young_KS.jpg" alt="The very young Kerry Shale" class="mh-70" /><br />
				<p class="font-smaller">The very young Kerry Shale</p>
			</div>
			<div class="text-center p-1 h-100 align-content-center">
				Leaving his home, family, girlfriend and car behind, he moved to London then. Kerry Shale described his father as a jokster who made jokes at the expenses of others and who could laugh 
				at his own jokes. Kerry Shale searched for distance to his father which helped him to discover his true self. He lived in Hampstead in London at first.
			</div>
			<div class="text-center p-1 h-100 align-content-center">
				<img src="/images/booklet/young_KS_2.jpg" alt="The young Kerry Shale" class="mh-70" /><br />
				<p class="font-smaller">The young Kerry Shale, ca. 1983</p>
			</div>
			<div class="text-center p-1 h-100 align-content-center">
				Kerry Shale then met the love of his life: Prof. Suzanne J. Gibson. It is not known when they had met the first time, they know each other at least since 1995. She is professor in ethics. 
				They married in 1996 and moved from Hampstead to Islington in London in July 1996. They both own Russian Blue cats.
			</div>
			<div class="text-center p-1 h-100 align-content-center">
				<img src="/images/booklet/KS_wife.jpg" alt="Kerry Shale's parents" class="mh-70" /><br />
				<p class="font-smaller">Kerry Shale and his wife Suzanne,<br />married since 25+ years</p>
			</div>
			<div class="text-center p-1 h-100 align-content-center">
				Kerry Shale has worked at The National Theatre, The Almeida, Hampstead, The Donmar Warehouse, Riverside Studios, The Gate and The Royal Court. He has done hundreds of radio plays for BBC.
				He has played with famous actors/actresses like Morgan Freeman, Barbra Streisand, Ralph Fiennes, Saul Rubinek, Michael J. Fox, Ray Liotta and many more.
			</div>
			<div class="text-center p-1 h-100 align-content-center">
				<img src="/images/booklet/older_KS.jpg" alt="The older Kerry Shale" class="mh-70" /><br />
				<p class="font-smaller">The fully grown Kerry Shale</p>
			</div>
			<div class="text-center p-1 h-100 align-content-center">
				To be continued...<br />❤
			</div>
			<div class="text-center p-1 h-100 align-content-center bg-black text-white">
				&nbsp;
			</div>
			<div class="text-center p-1 h-100 align-content-center bg-black text-white">
				&nbsp;
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>

